Mathematical source: Robert Sneiderman, A Candidate Proof of Finite Image
for Rank-Three Surface-Group Representations in Genus at Least Five,
public manuscript at commit 12f81e2852e0a8e71f16777d9eb9c7bc8916e6df:
https://github.com/Robby955/rank-three-mcg-finiteness

The candidate builds on Aaron Landesman and Daniel Litt's published work,
including Canonical representations of surface groups and Geometric local
systems on very general curves and isomonodromy. The present package's
scope and remaining interfaces are specified in OVERVIEW.md and
CORRESPONDENCE.md; it does not formalize those papers in full.

The formal proofs use Lean and mathlib. Mathlib is developed by the
mathlib community and is distributed under Apache-2.0. Dependencies are
fetched separately at the revisions in lake-manifest.json; their sources
and licenses remain with those projects. No dependency sources are
vendored in this package.
